# Auditor baseline for Advanced QFT and supersymmetry

Read-only inventory captured on 2026-10-23 before the builder handoff. This
file records existing suppliers and their actual boundaries; it does not
certify their proofs or modify any source.

## Scope and active-work boundary

`physics/CLAUDE.md`, `physics/SCHEMA.md`, `physics/WORKFLOW.md`,
`PHYSICS-CONTENT-MODEL.md`, `physics/README.md`, the existing QFT indexes, and
the owner direction were read before the audit. The owner authorizes a research
scaffold only: no production build, publication, or engine transition. The new
category must use a separate draft plan fragment and discovery track, and must
not edit `physics/research/plan-spec.json` or active manifests.

At audit start, HEAD was `c590df186d` (`Fix Fluid Dynamics category routes
with missing metadata`). The generated native status command for
`physics-frontier-expansion-2026-10-19` reported `running`, stage
`1-drift` at `0/1`, and no workers in flight. Its status directory is
`.autopilot/physics-frontier-expansion-2026-10-19`. Root separately confirmed
the corresponding physics state at
`physics/.physics-autopilot/physics-frontier-expansion-2026-10-19` also reports
`1-drift` with no workers in flight. The working tree already
had many independent edits, including `physics/research/plan-spec.json`; none
of those carriers was changed by this audit.

## Existing QFT inventory

The original QFT including QED research index records 177 proposed interfaces
on 31 A/B pairs (123 A-side and 54 B-side), with local arguments and
publication/acceptance explicitly separated. The 2026-10-19 QFT successor adds
27 pairs (81 A-side and 27 B-side interfaces), with 104 mathematical and four
physical interfaces. Its 108 item IDs and 54 page IDs have no intersection
with the original proposed inventory. These are research-plan records, not
proof acceptance for the successor's planned results.

The current library has published mathematical pages for the limited reused
interfaces below. Their actual page files were read and SHA-256 hashed during
this audit:

| Current page | Exact scope relevant here | Current page SHA-256 |
|---|---|---|
| `qftx-heavy-field-eft` | Positive Gaussian heavy-mode matching, a spectral derivative-expansion remainder under its low-momentum band and mass hypotheses, and Gaussian shell composition. This does not establish arbitrary interacting matching, massless thresholds, or all-regime EFT bounds. | `3e9c013c228be5dec1a3082d684fcc0990f601d16a21a162a84bf600a1720862` |
| `qftx-causal-renormalization` | Scalar finite-order causal extension and local finite-renormalization recursion. Gauge normalization is a separate obligation. | `576e67736555403773206f02caefc4ceaedb6549a1c7fccba8d7f51b09965573` |
| `qftx-renormalization-hopf` | Rooted-tree admissible-cut Hopf algebra, recursive antipode, and subtraction-character factorization. Graph-insertion and symmetry-factor identification are not automatic. | `dece2fb344e541c4568addd9440ec02c0e9239bc9e07f74b27da72812f679d5d` |
| `qftx-bv-brst` | Abelian jet BRST complex, nonminimal doublets, and a local first-anomaly obstruction class. No non-Abelian or all-order quantum gauge-normalization theorem. | `19450c1db97fa7e0cdb77c299b2e2c0c80def8353f5a5acef48baf81b089ee71` |
| `qftx-anomaly-cocycles` | Loop-Lie cocycle and conditional chiral/vectorlike charge-cancellation interfaces. Triangle descent, global anomalies, and a general Adler–Bardeen result are separate. | `1fc2ee7e5bf2ce4f90f9d8d3ecb18f4eb97dbabafbf6a7f4297039fe46d917cc` |
| `qftx-hall-bps-wall-crossing` | A finite-hereditary-quiver Hall factorization and spectrum-generator identity. It is not physical four-dimensional supersymmetric BPS counting. | `65d60a3a41833f387482161f1579b09536956d5d38688a2ba9376835af3c6dc3` |
| `qftx-categorified-line-operators` | Rouquier braid action, grading, and Euler decategorification. A physical defect realization functor is additional data. | `6911981d6045d9b709a92af41dfe9550692287cce9f18428988fae7379a52e07` |
