           "id": "thm-csm-frontier-swendsen-wang-invariance",
           "kind": "theorem",
           "domain": "mathematics",
-          "title": "Finite Swendsen–Wang update preserves the Potts law",
-          "statement": "For a finite simple graph $G=(V,E)$, integer $Q\\geq2$, and finite activities $v_e\\geq0$, let $\\pi_P(\\sigma)=w_P(\\sigma)/Z_P$ be the normalized finite Potts law and let the Swendsen–Wang update be the two-stage procedure of activating equal-spin edges with probabilities $v_e/(1+v_e)$ and independently recoloring each resulting component uniformly from $[Q]$. Its transition kernel preserves $\\pi_P$. The procedure always terminates after finitely many edge and component operations. No irreducibility, uniqueness, convergence-rate, or critical-mixing claim is made.",
+          "title": "Finite Swendsen\u2013Wang update preserves the Potts law",
