           },
-          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and the finite-matrix $C^*$-identity used by the quasi-local completion. Let $\\mathcal A$ be the quasi-local algebra of uniformly finite-dimensional spins on $\\mathbb Z^d$, $d\\ge1$, with max-coordinate distance $d_\\infty$. Let $\\alpha_t$ be a strongly continuous automorphism group satisfying the exponential Lieb–Robinson estimate\n\n$$\\|[A,\\alpha_t(B)]\\|\\le\\frac{2\\|A\\|\\|B\\|}{C}(e^{v|t|}-1)\\sum_{x\\in X,\\,y\\in Y}F_a(d_\\infty(x,y)),\\qquad F_a(r)=e^{-ar}(1+r)^{-d-1},$$\n\nfor disjoint finite nonempty $X,Y$, $A\\in\\mathcal A_X$, $B\\in\\mathcal A_Y$, all real $t$, and fixed $a,C>0$, $v\\ge0$. In particular this holds for the thermodynamic dynamics of a bounded finite-range interaction $\\Phi$, with $C=C_{F_a}$ and $v=2C\\|\\Phi\\|_{F_a}/\\hbar$ from the weighted commutator theorem and any $\\hbar>0$.\n\nHere a **positive-energy ground state** means an algebraic state $\\eta$ admitting a contractive unital $*$-representation $\\pi$ on a complex Hilbert space, a unit vector $\\Omega$, and a strongly continuous unitary group $U_t$ fixing $\\Omega$, such that $\\eta(A)=\\langle\\pi(A)\\Omega,\\Omega\\rangle$, $\\pi(\\alpha_t(A))=U_t\\pi(A)U_t^*$, and the generator is $iK$ for a positive self-adjoint densely defined $K$. Inner products are linear in their first argument. Such a representation can be restricted to the cyclic subspace generated by $\\Omega$; no spectral resolution is included in the definition.\n\nSuppose $\\omega$ is the unique positive-energy ground state and its cyclic ground representation has an infinite-volume energy gap $\\gamma>0$: writing $H=\\hbar K$, require\n\n$$\\sigma(K)\\subseteq\\{0\\}\\cup[g,\\infty),\\qquad g=\\gamma/\\hbar>0.$$\n\nThen for every pair of disjoint finite nonempty supports, with $r=\\operatorname{dist}_\\infty(X,Y)\\ge1$, one has\n\n$$|\\omega(AB)-\\omega(A)\\omega(B)|\\le\\|A\\|\\|B\\|\\left(\\frac{2|X||Y|}{\\pi C}+1+\\frac{2v+g}{\\pi a g r}\\right)e^{-\\mu r},\\qquad \\mu=\\frac{ag}{2v+g}>0.$$\n\nThis is exponential connected clustering for the infinite-volume state. The hypotheses do not require uniformly gapped finite-volume approximations, translation invariance, or a particular choice of finite-volume boundary ground states. The same estimate holds for any positive-energy state representation with $\\ker K=\\mathbb C\\Omega$ and the stated gap, even without uniqueness among all ground states. Uniqueness is a sufficient hypothesis for that kernel condition, proved below. For other weighted interactions the assertion applies whenever their strongly continuous dynamics and the displayed Lieb–Robinson estimate are supplied; no missing thermodynamic-existence theorem for a general interaction is assumed to have been proved here.\n\nFor physical bookkeeping $t$ is in seconds, $H,\\gamma$ are in joules, $\\hbar$ is in joule-seconds and $K,g,v$ have inverse-second units. Lattice distances, $a,C,\\mu$ and the exponential argument are dimensionless. The theorem does not prove a gap or uniqueness for an unspecified physical model.",
+          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and the finite-matrix $C^*$-identity used by the quasi-local completion. Let $\\mathcal A$ be the quasi-local algebra of uniformly finite-dimensional spins on $\\mathbb Z^d$, $d\\ge1$, with max-coordinate distance $d_\\infty$. Let $\\alpha_t$ be a strongly continuous automorphism group satisfying the exponential Lieb\u2013Robinson estimate\n\n$$\\|[A,\\alpha_t(B)]\\|\\le\\frac{2\\|A\\|\\|B\\|}{C}(e^{v|t|}-1)\\sum_{x\\in X,\\,y\\in Y}F_a(d_\\infty(x,y)),\\qquad F_a(r)=e^{-ar}(1+r)^{-d-1},$$\n\nfor disjoint finite nonempty $X,Y$, $A\\in\\mathcal A_X$, $B\\in\\mathcal A_Y$, all real $t$, and fixed $a,C>0$, $v\\ge0$. In particular this holds for the thermodynamic dynamics of a bounded finite-range interaction $\\Phi$, with $C=C_{F_a}$ and $v=2C\\|\\Phi\\|_{F_a}/\\hbar$ from the weighted commutator theorem and any $\\hbar>0$.\n\nHere a **positive-energy ground state** means an algebraic state $\\eta$ admitting a contractive unital $*$-representation $\\pi$ on a complex Hilbert space, a unit vector $\\Omega$, and a strongly continuous unitary group $U_t$ fixing $\\Omega$, such that $\\eta(A)=\\langle\\pi(A)\\Omega,\\Omega\\rangle$, $\\pi(\\alpha_t(A))=U_t\\pi(A)U_t^*$, and the generator is $iK$ for a positive self-adjoint densely defined $K$. Inner products are linear in their first argument. Such a representation can be restricted to the cyclic subspace generated by $\\Omega$; no spectral resolution is included in the definition.\n\nSuppose $\\omega$ is the unique positive-energy ground state and its cyclic ground representation has an infinite-volume energy gap $\\gamma>0$: writing $H=\\hbar K$, require\n\n$$\\sigma(K)\\subseteq\\{0\\}\\cup[g,\\infty),\\qquad g=\\gamma/\\hbar>0.$$\n\nThen for every pair of disjoint finite nonempty supports, with $r=\\operatorname{dist}_\\infty(X,Y)\\ge1$, one has\n\n$$|\\omega(AB)-\\omega(A)\\omega(B)|\\le\\|A\\|\\|B\\|\\left(\\frac{2|X||Y|}{\\pi C}+1+\\frac{2v+g}{\\pi a g r}\\right)e^{-\\mu r},\\qquad \\mu=\\frac{ag}{2v+g}>0.$$\n\nThis is exponential connected clustering for the infinite-volume state. The hypotheses do not require uniformly gapped finite-volume approximations, translation invariance, or a particular choice of finite-volume boundary ground states. The same estimate holds for any positive-energy state representation with $\\ker K=\\mathbb C\\Omega$ and the stated gap, even without uniqueness among all ground states. Uniqueness is a sufficient hypothesis for that kernel condition, proved below. For other weighted interactions the assertion applies whenever their strongly continuous dynamics and the displayed Lieb\u2013Robinson estimate are supplied; no missing thermodynamic-existence theorem for a general interaction is assumed to have been proved here.\n\nFor physical bookkeeping $t$ is in seconds, $H,\\gamma$ are in joules, $\\hbar$ is in joule-seconds and $K,g,v$ have inverse-second units. Lattice distances, $a,C,\\mu$ and the exponential argument are dimensionless. The theorem does not prove a gap or uniqueness for an unspecified physical model.",
           "reference": "items/thm-qsmx-gapped-ground-state-clustering.md",
           "design_state": "Step 2 owner-authorized same-pair local proof; source release recorded, ordinary native gates pending."
         },
