-          "statement": "Use natural units $c=\\hbar=k_B=1$. Thus energy $E$ has units $\\mathrm{s^{-1}}$, inverse temperature $\\beta$ and the positive model parameter $C$ have units $\\mathrm{s}$, and $S_0\\in\\mathbb R$ is dimensionless. In this item, **JT disk model** means only the disk-sector spectral model with the density specified below; the label refers to the cited two-dimensional Jackiw–Teitelboim calculations and adopts no additional field equation or path-integral construction. **Genus-zero disk contribution** means the single connected disk term, with one boundary and no handles, in the formal expansion by spacetime topology. A **nonperturbative completion** means additional exact model data that select an exact theory beyond the terms fixed by that formal expansion.\n\nA **continuous spectral density** here is a nonnegative function $\\rho_0:(0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$ whose measure $\\rho_0(E)\\,dE$ assigns model spectral weight to energy intervals. Adopt\n\n$$\\rho_0(E):=e^{S_0}\\frac{C}{2\\pi^2}\\sinh\\!\\left(2\\pi\\sqrt{2CE}\\right),\\qquad E>0.$$\n\nThe density has units $\\mathrm{s}$, so $\\rho_0(E)\\,dE$ is dimensionless. This postulate specifies a continuous disk-level input only. It does not specify an individual discrete energy spectrum, sum higher-topology terms, choose a nonperturbative completion, or assert that the model describes nature.",
